    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00030",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Insurance costs",
      "ordinal": 30,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00031",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Revenue generated",
      "ordinal": 31,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00032",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Revenue generated",
      "ordinal": 32,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00033",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "LCC can provide a flexible approach to costing, where buyers can focus on specific areas of the lifecycle which will have the greatest impact.",
      "ordinal": 33,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00034",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Whole Life Costing",
      "ordinal": 34,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00035",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This is a technique to calculate the total cost value of goods or services over their full useful life , from cradle to grave, taking into account all the total relevant costs of purchasing, operating, maintaining and disposal which can include, but is not limited to the costs listed above.",
      "ordinal": 35,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00036",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Unlike LCC which may consider only part of the costs, a WLC approach should consider all the relevant costs relating to the goods or services.",
      "ordinal": 36,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00037",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Information for Bidders",
      "ordinal": 37,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00038",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where LCC or WLC are being used to assess the costs of a contract, organisations must establish the method in advance and share with bidders:",
      "ordinal": 38,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00039",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "the method that will be used",
      "ordinal": 39,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00040",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "any assumptions which have been made",
      "ordinal": 40,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00041",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "what information is required from bidders.",
      "ordinal": 41,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00042",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The costing method being used must be objective , based on non-discriminatory criteria , accessible to all interested parties and not favour a particular bidder.",
      "ordinal": 42,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00043",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where any common methods have been made mandatory by legislation, they must be used e.g. the clean vehicles Directive requires that energy and environmental impacts linked to the operation of vehicles over their whole lifetime are taken into account in all purchases of road transport vehicles, as covered by the public procurement Directives and “The Cleaner Road Transport Vehicles (Scotland) Regulations 2010”.",
      "ordinal": 43,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Information for Bidders"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00044",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors",
      "ordinal": 44,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00045",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Costs attributable to environmental factors linked to goods or services during their life cycle can be considered where the financial value can be determined and verified in an objective and non-discriminatory way.",
      "ordinal": 45,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00046",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "T he data required from bidders must be accessible by all and gathered without unnecessary burden.",
      "ordinal": 46,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00047",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Tools and Guidance",
      "ordinal": 47,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00048",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Please find below links to resources which may be useful in building cost models, providing considerations and guidance:",
      "ordinal": 48,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00049",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Scottish Futures Trust (SFT) Whole Life Appraisal Tool",
      "ordinal": 49,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00050",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Produced for the Scottish Government in response to the Review of Public Sector Procurement in Construction 2013, the SFT provided guidance and a whole life appraisal tool which, although created from a construction perspective, may provide information and models useful for complex service contracts. Buyers may also find further information on whole life costing and sustainability in chapter 11 and 18 of the Construction Procurement Handbook .",
      "ordinal": 50,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00051",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Should Cost Modelling",
      "ordinal": 51,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00052",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "UK GCF developed an extensive suite of guidance, tools and templates on “ Should Cost Modelling ” (SCM), a term used to describe Whole Life Cost Modelling. SCM can provide a forecast of what a service, project or programme ‘should’ cost over its whole life, provide a structure for bids to be received, support the evaluation of bids (including helping to identify abnormally low bids), and provide a baseline to compare forecasted costs to the actuals during the contract performance.",
      "ordinal": 52,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00053",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Whole Life Costing (+CO2)",
      "ordinal": 53,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00054",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Forum for the Future in partnership with Fife Council developed a Whole Life Costing (+CO2) tool and guidance , which may be helpful to assess the whole life costs including CO2 emissions (from point of purchase to end of life (but does not include embedded or embodied carbon incurred during supply chain activities)) of any product or service which consumes electricity, gas, oil, vehicle fuel and/or water. As above, any method to calculate emissions must be determined and verified in an objective and non-discriminatory way , accessible by all bidders and gathered without unnecessary burden.",
      "ordinal": 54,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00055",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Knowledgehub",
      "ordinal": 55,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00056",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Knowledgehub is a free service where public sector buyers can find helpful guidance, templates and share best practice which includes information on costing models.",
      "ordinal": 56,
      "heading_path": [
        "Life Cycle Impact Mapping",
        "Life Cycle Costing",
        "Whole Life Costing",
        "Costs Attributable to Environmental Factors"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
